# Scan: (SANE, which talks to scanners, is in 45.) Tesseract reads the text (English, plus the languages most used
# in Europe; more are one package away: tesseract-ocr-<language>); OpenCV finds a page's corners in a photo.
tesseract-ocr
tesseract-ocr-eng
tesseract-ocr-deu
tesseract-ocr-fra
tesseract-ocr-spa
tesseract-ocr-ita
tesseract-ocr-nor
python3-opencv
# Machines: QEMU with KVM, its disk tools, UEFI firmware (with Secure Boot) and a software TPM for Windows 11.
qemu-system-x86
qemu-utils
ovmf
swtpm
swtpm-tools
# Tempo: FluidSynth renders the General MIDI instruments from a sound font; numpy (already in) and SciPy's filters
# do the rest (the effects, the mixer's EQ and compressor run through scipy.signal.lfilter).
python3-scipy
fluidsynth
fluid-soundfont-gm
# Tempo's plugins (LV2, hosted through lilv: apps/huginn_tempo_lv2.py): LSP's studio effects, Calf's (and its
# synth and organ), x42's, Dragonfly's reverbs, AVL's sampled drum kits and setBfree's tonewheel organ.
# (ZAM's are left out: 165 MB for effects these already cover.)
python3-lilv
# LV2's own descriptions (what a reverb, an instrument, an analyser is): Ubuntu has them only in lv2-dev (1 MB).
lv2-dev
lsp-plugins-lv2
calf-plugins
x42-plugins
dragonfly-reverb-lv2
avldrums.lv2
setbfree
